// Lily# (2026-10-20, lysc Release): an arpeggio in a second voice is drawn at the wrong column. Below,
// the lower voice's <d' f' a'>8@arpeggio is its third event (at 3/8); the wiggle is drawn before the
// f'8 at 2/8 instead, the column of the upper voice's third event (r8). ArpeggioEngraver resolves the
// item's X with GetItemXOffset(measures, MeasureIndex, ItemIndex), the voice's own item index looked
// up in the staff's measure items, it seems. Found by the OMR's generated pieces (OmrGen --arpeggios):
// piano004's right hand, voice { ... } { d4 fis8 <d fis>8@arpeggio <cis e>4. r8 }.
title "arpeggio in a second voice"
octave absolute
time 4/4
key c major

part p1 { clef treble }

section Piece {
  p1 {
    voice { r8 g'''8 r8 e'''8 c'''2 } { d''4 f''8 <d'' f'' a''>8@arpeggio <c'' e''>2 } |
  }
}

form { ~Piece }

score {
  staff p1 "Staff"
}
